hi i'm gayle simmons and we're making  spaghetti pie when i was 19 years old i  traveled to new zealand and australia  for the summer with my best friend and  college roommate camille one thing that  we noticed on our travels was that at  every truck stop they always had  spaghetti sandwiches which we thought  was pretty incredible this was long  before the carbs are scary days but it  was so delicious and i've always thought  about that sandwich i've never really  attempted to make my own but played  around a little bit in the kitchen and  came up with what i think is even better  the spaghetti pie i'm putting in a can  of whole tomatoes here and i'm going to  break them up a little bit you know  tongs are like an extended part of my  arm these whole tomatoes have so much  flavor and just the right amount of  liquid with them that you want as  opposed to a can of crushed tomatoes  where you kind of just get less tomato  flesh you want it to simmer for about  five minutes to reduce some of that  liquid and thicken the mixture but you  definitely want to make sure that  there's still a good amount of sauce  from cooking so much i've learned a few  things you definitely want enough salt  that the water tastes salty i mean you  don't want to dump a bucket of salt but  i estimate two tablespoons of salt for a  pound of pasta i just want to have great  food around at all times this is just  sort of perfect for everything it feeds  more people than you can believe it's  big  and it's rich and it's super delicious  it's easy to make and it feeds a lot of  people so don't think that you only have  to use it when you're cooking for 10  people i make it it feeds four and then  i put it in the fridge and i'm happy to  eat it for lunch i'm happy for my  daughter to have it for lunch eat it  late night as i said i find lots of  reasons to eat this buy no being shy  with the cheese  my mother was actually a cooking teacher  so when i was growing up i spent a lot  of time in the kitchen with her cooking  she taught cooking in our kitchen to  women in the neighborhood so i have a  lot of early memories of watching her  cook and eating the food that she would  make for her little cooking school we  ate a lot of unusual ingredients that  most kids didn't eat but truthfully when  i was growing up all i really wanted was  a hot dog and some mac and cheese like  everyone else could eat for lunch and my  mom was making zucchini and shadro i  don't know there was some weird stuff  but it was amazing and ultimately set me  on a horse  that made me who i am and obviously  taught me what i wanted to do the most  in my life but at the time you didn't  realize it the last thing you want when  you're graduating from college is for  everyone to tell you that you're just  like your mother and now i embrace it  it's like i couldn't run for my own  destiny you know  doesn't look ridiculously delicious  [Music]  just as good i remember  it still works  [Music]
 

